lobal500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2026, "rank": 151, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2026, "rank": 54, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2026, "rank": 53, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2026, "rank": 19, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "aiq", "title": "Fortune AIQ 50", "year": 2025, "rank": 49, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2025, "rank": 147, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2025, "rank": 51, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": 22, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": 19, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 149, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500--household-products", "title": "Fortune Sector Leaders: Household Products", "year": 2024, "rank": 1, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 50, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": 22, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": 18, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": 24, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 154, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": 44, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 51, "itemDescription": "The consumer packaged goods giant Procter &amp; Gamble, famous for products ranging from Tide detergent to Pepto Bismol, saw revenue increase 5% in 2022, to $80.2 billion.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>As inflation raged in 2022 and into 2023, P&amp;G was among the most prominent companies criticized by consumer activists for \u201cgreedflation,\u201d as it repeatedly raised prices for consumers in attempts to offset its own rising costs.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>P&amp;G raised its year-end sales outlook in April 2023 from a 1% decline to a 1% increase, a sign it believes it\u2019s turned the corner on inflation.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>The company is diversifying away from traditional retail channels; its e-commerce sales grew 11% in 2022 and now make up 14% of total sales.</li><br />\r\n</ul>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2022, "rank": 23, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 154, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 47, "itemDescription": "<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Procter &amp; Gamble makes and sells familiar household brands such as Tide laundry detergent, Gillette razors, Crest toothpaste, and Old Spice deodorant. Like other consumer goods giants, P&amp;G has faced a tricky balancing act: It is benefiting from rising sales in a recovering economy (it brought in $76.1 billion in revenue in its last fiscal year, a 7.3% increase from the year prior) while also striving to protect its profit margins from inflation. The company also faced a potential self-inflicted wound going into 2022: The detection of benzene, a potential carcinogen, in some of its aerosol deodorants led P&amp;G to institute a recall in November 2021, and the problem has since prompted multiple lawsuits. </span>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2021, "rank": 21, "itemDescription": "&nbsp;"}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 128, "itemDescription": "The consumer products giant emerged from the COVID-19 crisis with strong profits, exceeding its own fiscal year 2020 goals with 6% organic sales growth and 13% core earnings-per-share growth. That was partially thanks to a spike in demand for home-goods brands like Charmin, Bounty, Downy, and more. Procter &amp; Gamble experienced a substantial leap in revenue almost across the board, including net sales of $19.7 billion in the second quarter of fiscal year 2021, up 8% from the year before. P&amp;G\u2019s share price has weathered market volatility, rising 15.4% from March 2, 2020, through May 24, 2021. The company even increased its quarterly dividend by 10% in April 2021, making this the 65th consecutive year that P&amp;G has boosted its dividend."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 43, "itemDescription": "The consumer products giant emerged from the COVID-19 crisis with strong profits, exceeding its own fiscal year 2020 goals with 6% organic sales growth and 13% core earnings-per-share growth. That was partially thanks to a spike in demand for home-goods brands like Charmin, Bounty, Downy, and more. Procter &amp; Gamble experienced a substantial leap in revenue almost across the board, including net sales of $19.7 billion in the second quarter of fiscal year 2021, up 8% from the year before. P&amp;G\u2019s share price has weathered market volatility, rising 15.4% from March 2, 2020, through May 24, 2021. The company even increased its quarterly dividend by 10% in April 2021, making this the 65th consecutive year that P&amp;G has boosted its dividend."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2020, "rank": 23, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 156, "itemDescription": "The consumer products giant emerged from a major reorganization in 2019 and ended the calendar year with an optimistic outlook for investors across the board, including net sales of $17.8 billion in the first quarter of fiscal year 2020, up 7% from the year before. What would be welcome news during normal times became a bulwark in the age of the novel coronavirus. P&amp;G\u2019s share price weathered the stock market volatility that marked the early weeks of the pandemic\u2019s spread, and even as other companies cut their quarterly dividends, P&amp;G made its payout for its 64th consecutive year."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 50, "itemDescription": "The consumer products giant emerged from a major reorganization in 2019 and ended the calendar year with an optimistic outlook for investors across the board, including net sales of $17.8 billion in the first quarter of fiscal year 2020, up 7% from the year before. What would be welcome news during normal times became a bulwark in the age of the novel coronavirus. P&amp;G\u2019s share price weathered the stock market volatility that marked the early weeks of the pandemic\u2019s spread, and even as other companies cut their quarterly dividends, P&amp;G made its payout for its 64th consecutive year."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2019, "rank": 31, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 146, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 45, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2018, "rank": 34, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 13